  <!-- Introduction -->
  <h2 id="introduction">The Streaming Geo-Restriction Problem</h2>
  <p>
    You're in a hotel in Barcelona, ready to unwind with your favorite Netflix show—only to discover it's not available
    in Spain. Or you're on a long flight with WiFi, but your Hulu subscription is useless outside the US. Sound
    familiar?
  </p>
  <p>
    Streaming services use geo-restrictions to comply with regional licensing agreements. Your Netflix library in the UK
    looks completely different from what you'd see at home in the US. Disney+ originals might launch months later in
    certain countries. BBC iPlayer is completely blocked outside Britain.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>A VPN solves this problem.</strong> By connecting through a server in your home country, streaming services
    see that location instead of your actual one. Your US Netflix library travels with you to Europe, Asia, or anywhere
    else you roam.
  </p>
  <p>
    We tested 10 VPNs specifically for streaming performance—checking which platforms they unblock, measuring speeds
    from multiple countries, and evaluating reliability over weeks of real-world travel.
  </p>

