  <p>
    Not all VPNs work well for streaming. Here's what separates the best from the rest:
  </p>

  <h3>Streaming Server Network</h3>
  <p>
    VPNs need servers in the countries whose content you want to access. More importantly, they need servers that
    actually work with streaming platforms. Netflix and others actively block VPN IP addresses—good VPNs constantly
    rotate their IPs to stay ahead.
  </p>

  <h3>Speed and Reliability</h3>
  <p>
    Streaming requires consistent bandwidth. A VPN that works but buffers constantly isn't useful. Look for VPNs with
    minimal speed loss (under 20%) and stable connections that don't drop during your show.
  </p>

  <h3>Platform Compatibility</h3>
  <p>
    The best streaming VPNs work across Netflix, Disney+, Hulu, BBC iPlayer, Amazon Prime Video, HBO Max, and more.
    Some VPNs work great with Netflix but fail on Disney+. We tested all major platforms.
  </p>

  <h3>Multiple Device Support</h3>
  <p>
    You might stream on your laptop, phone, tablet, or smart TV. The best VPNs cover all devices under one subscription
    and offer native apps for each platform.
  </p>

  <h3>Smart DNS (Bonus Feature)</h3>
  <p>
    Some VPNs include Smart DNS, which unblocks streaming on devices that don't support VPN apps (like older smart TVs).
    This feature routes only the location-checking traffic through the VPN, potentially offering faster speeds.
  </p>

